            <ArticleTitle>Do shoes matter? A story of shoes in the neonatal intensive care unit.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/NNA.0b013e31818fe652</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Faced with an increase in foot-related absences and complaints of foot pain by staff, a nurse manager sought help from the nursing research department staff to help find answers to this problem. The authors discuss how replacing the shoes that the nurses wore to a walker-style shoe was able to improve not only the foot pain but also the unit's health as well.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
